1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,800
ResearchAgent gives coding agents a research wallet.

2
00:00:02,800 --> 00:00:05,600
Ask a question and set a budget.

3
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:06,800
Paid on delivery.

4
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:08,400
Proven on the ledger.

5
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:15,262
How does the writer get paid, and what
stops the agent from reading the article

6
00:00:15,262 --> 00:00:17,400
and then refusing to pay?

7
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:18,600
Free sources first.

8
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:21,800
Policy buys the missing passage within your budget.

9
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:26,200
This run bought one S$0.40 article.

10
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:32,200
The key that unlocks the article is the same key
that releases the writer's payment.

11
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:39,600
The writer collects by publishing the article key.

12
00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:44,800
This browser reads both transactions from a
public node and hashes the key.

13
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:46,800
It matches the payment lock.

14
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:54,600
Check the recorded proof without asking a question.

15
00:00:54,600 --> 00:01:00,600
The featured run shows all five gates held:
twenty-four checks passed and two not checked.

16
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:09,000
Export the receipts and check them outside the app.

17
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:12,200
Our TypeScript and Python verifiers
were written separately.

18
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:15,800
The receipts tie the cited passages to the payment.

19
00:01:19,400 --> 00:01:23,800
The writer view links accepted operator-issued
Credentials to the writer wallet.

20
00:01:23,800 --> 00:01:28,200
Follow the identity record and the
payment directly from the app.

21
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:33,400
Only policy code can pay.

22
00:01:33,400 --> 00:01:36,200
The language model cannot raise the budget.

23
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:40,200
The five-second plan sheet confirms how
the research will proceed.

24
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:47,000
Claude Code uses the same research tools over MCP.

25
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:52,200
The spending caps come from the environment;
the calling model can't raise them.

26
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:55,400
The result includes cited
passages and payment links.

27
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:06,600
From a question to a paid passage, in
the browser or Claude Code.

28
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:07,800
Paid on delivery.

29
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:09,400
Proven on the ledger.

30
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:10,600
Check it yourself.

31
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:13,000
The key matches the payment lock.
